<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Münster</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1648</span> · Also known as Treaty of Münster · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of Münster was the treaty signed in Münster on 30 January 1648 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, one of the settlements of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a>. It ended the Eighty Years' War, with Spain recognising the independence of the United Provinces. It also confirmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> conquests, including northern Brabant, and the closure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a>, which harmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peace-of-munster.jpg" alt="Peace of Münster" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gerard ter Borch · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Westfaelischer_Friede_in_Muenster_(Gerard_Terborch_1648).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
